{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Baseline the increment on Java 17 and Spring Framework 6.x as stated in the specification, keeping the existing Gradle-based build and Bamboo CI setup implied by the user stories.",
    "U2: Implement an HDFS-backed module registry: custom module uber-jars are uploaded to a configurable HDFS directory (e.g., /xd/modules); newly arriving containers resolve modules from HDFS using the Apache Hadoop FileSystem API, copy them to a local staging directory, and load them with an isolated module classloader. Since HDFS has no native watch facility, containers poll the registry directory on a configurable interval (with checksum/timestamp comparison) to detect new or updated modules.",
    "U3: Implement the native WebSocket sink on top of Spring's spring-websocket support running on the embedded servlet container, exposing module options for path, port, and message handling, and supporting full-duplex text and binary frames over a single TCP connection.",
    "U8: Introduce a shared dependency location (xd/lib) loaded by a common parent classloader shared by all module classloaders (parent-first delegation); modules that require conflicting versions of a shared jar bundle that jar inside the module uber-jar to override the shared copy, matching the stated current recommendation.",
    "U5: Replace the Bamboo Artifactory Gradle plugin task with a Bamboo command task that invokes ./gradlew; enable distributed JVM tests, run the suite with embedded Hadoop disabled via a dedicated Gradle test profile, and tune maxParallelForks based on agent vCPU count.",
    "U4/U6: Evaluate npm-cache for dependency caching in the build and adopt it if the front-end build is affected; configure SonarQube quality gates and Bamboo/Sonar integration so the committer who introduced a violation is notified automatically.",
    "U7: Provision Windows CI on the existing Bamboo environment: configure a Windows agent with PowerShell access, install and script required services (Redis, RabbitMQ) as Windows services via PowerShell, and add a commit-triggered Bamboo plan that runs the integration test suite."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "An existing Spring XD-like distributed runtime codebase, Gradle build, Bamboo CI server running on EC2, and an available HDFS/Hadoop cluster with client libraries are already in place; this increment extends them rather than building from scratch.",
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are hands-on work-hours only and exclude elapsed waiting time (e.g., long unattended CI runs, provisioning lead times).",
    "A Windows machine/agent and PowerShell access can be obtained within the Bamboo environment without procurement effort beyond what is estimated.",
    "Unit and integration tests are expected for new features (HDFS registry, WebSocket sink, xd/lib support) and are estimated as separate activities.",
    "The WARN-log increase (U6) is caused by a bounded set of PMD/Sonar violations fixable within the estimated effort; no large-scale architectural refactoring is required.",
    "Documentation deliverable for U1 targets the existing documentation format/toolchain (e.g., Asciidoc/Markdown in the project repo) and includes module structure, packaging as uber-jar, and deployment guidance.",
    "Standard development activities such as code review, defect fixing, and release verification are included as explicit WBS activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment planning, requirements analysis, and high-level design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze the eight user stories, reconcile them against the existing runtime and build system, produce the high-level design (HDFS module registry, WebSocket sink, xd/lib shared classloading, CI changes), and define acceptance criteria and task breakdown for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Custom module development documentation",
      "activity_description": "Write developer-facing documentation describing recommended standards and patterns for building custom modules: project layout, build configuration, packaging as an uber-jar, shared dependency handling via xd/lib, and deployment to HDFS-backed containers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: HDFS-hosted custom module registry implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement upload and resolution of custom module uber-jars in HDFS: configurable registry directory, Hadoop FileSystem-based access, container-side polling and change detection, local staging of jars, isolated module classloading, logging, and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 80
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U2: HDFS registry unit and integration tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests plus integration tests using MiniDFSCluster (or equivalent) covering upload, discovery by newly arriving containers, update detection, corrupted/missing jar handling, and concurrent access.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U3: Native WebSocket sink implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the native WebSocket sink module using Spring WebSocket on the embedded container: full-duplex text/binary messaging over a single TCP connection, module options (path, port), connection lifecycle management, and integration with the stream sink contract.",
      "most_likely_effort": 56
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U3: WebSocket sink tests and module packaging",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests for the WebSocket sink (client/server round-trip, binary and text frames, reconnect behavior) and package it as a deployable module.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U4: CI options research (npm-cache evaluation)",
      "activity_description": "Research CI options to improve build stability and reliability, with a hands-on evaluation of npm-cache for caching previously installed npm dependencies; document findings and, if applicable, wire the chosen option into the build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U5: EC2 CI build improvements (Gradle and Bamboo tasks)",
      "activity_description": "Enable distributed JVM tests, replace the Artifactory Gradle task with a Bamboo command task invoking ./gradlew, configure and validate a test profile with embedded Hadoop off, and turn on/tune maxParallelForks; verify builds run reliably on EC2 agents with functional assertions intact.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U6: WARN log investigation and PMD/Sonar violation remediation",
      "activity_description": "Investigate the increase in WARN logs, fix the underlying PMD/Sonar violations (or adjust log levels/rules where appropriate), and configure Sonar so the responsible committer is automatically notified of new violations.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "U7: Windows CI infrastructure on Bamboo",
      "activity_description": "Set up automated integration tests on Windows in the existing Bamboo environment: obtain PowerShell access, install and script required services (Redis, RabbitMQ, etc.), author the Windows CI task, and hook it to commit-triggered builds.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U8: Shared dependency location (xd/lib) support",
      "activity_description": "Implement a common shared location (xd/lib) whose jars are loaded by a shared parent classloader for all custom modules, including the documented escape hatch of bundling conflicting versions inside a module uber-jar; update runtime startup and related docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Increment-level integration/system testing and defect fixing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end scenarios across the increment (module build per U1 docs, HDFS deployment, WebSocket sink streaming, shared xd/lib dependencies) on Linux and Windows CI, triage and fix defects.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Release packaging, deployment verification, and final documentation",
      "activity_description": "Produce the release build, verify CI pipelines (EC2 and Windows) are green, finalize release notes and cross-references between feature code and documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 460
  }
}
